---
source: tests/cli/basics.rs
expression: "format!(\"usage: {listed}\")"
---
usage: fetchloom [options] <command>

examples:
  fetchloom add iris    # in a project folder, pick an iris dataset to add
  fetchloom add geo:GSE60450    # a GEO series, by its accession
  fetchloom add ../measurements    # files on this machine, no network needed
  fetchloom sync    # in a clone, put the files data.lock lists in data/

commands:
  add          add a dataset to the project and download it into the data folder
  remove       remove a dataset and the files fetchloom placed for it
  exclude      leave files out of their dataset for good, such as bad samples
  drop         free a dataset's space here, keeping it in data.lock
  sync         put the files data.lock lists into the data folder
  lock         update data.lock from data.toml, without changing the data folder
  status       list files that are missing, changed locally or extra
  audit        ask the sources if data.lock's files are still served or changed
  diff         show what data.lock and its file lists changed between commits
  list         list the project's datasets: source, size and folder
  export       write the SHA-256 or link of each file, or citations of datasets
  push         copy the files data.lock lists into a folder or S3 bucket mirror
  path         print where a dataset or a file in it is, syncing it if needed
  cache        show the cache, free what no project needs, or verify it
  settings     show each setting, or change one in the settings file
  get          download a dataset once, without a project
  search       find datasets on hugging face, kaggle, zenodo, GEO and more
  auth         sign in for private data, or data with terms to accept
  completions  print a script that completes fetchloom's commands in a shell
  help         explain the ideas behind fetchloom, or one command

global options:
  -q, --quiet         print only the answer, warnings and errors
  -v, --verbose...    say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug logs
      --json          print one JSON document on stdout, not the usual output
      --progress      with --json, keep plain progress lines on stderr
      --offline       use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes           answer yes to questions, but never pick a dataset for you
      --color <when>  when to use color: auto, the default, always or never
  -C <dir>            run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
      --mirror <url>  ask the mirror at this folder, web address or S3 bucket,
                      as `s3://bucket/prefix`, or
                      `s3:https://host:port/bucket/prefix` at another service,
                      for files before their sources. repeat it for more
      --no-config     leave the settings file unread for this run
  -h, --help          print help: -h the common part, --help all of it
  -V, --version       print the version

help topics: `fetchloom help concepts`, `environment` or `exit-codes`
for agents and scripts: `fetchloom help agents`, what --json and exit codes say
R and python helpers: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom/user/reference/
docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom/
report a bug: https://github.com/nikhil-yn-aix/fetchloom/issues
